%% SCOPE: Manager selects an existing sport. New sport is rejected before transaction with 403.
%% authorizeExact(MANAGER) rejects ADMIN and RECEPTIONIST for this operational endpoint.
%% B is the actual internal helper, not another HTTP endpoint or a separate service.
%% DB read messages aggregate verified Prisma queries. Validators short-circuit on the first error.
%% Short-circuit checks skip later validation reads when an earlier validator throws.
%% Database failures roll back the enclosing transaction and propagate through errorHandler.
%% UI omits termId. Server auto-selects covering non-CLOSED facility or global terms.
%% Client-invalid forms show validation errors without making this API request.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Center Manager
    participant UI as API client
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as schedulesController
    participant S as schedulesService
    participant B as createScheduleBatchInTx
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL
    A->>UI: Select sport, class, room, Coaches and date slots
    UI->>UI: Prepare request timestamps, unmounted ActivityPlanner uses +07:00
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/class-schedules/activity-plan
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorizeExact(MANAGER), validate request
    alt request rejected
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403
    else request accepted
        API->>C: createActivityPlan(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: createActivityPlan(body, false)
        activate S
        alt sport.mode new
            S-->>C: 403 Admin must create the sport first
        else existing sport selected
            S->>DB: Begin transaction, read room and active Coach profiles
            DB-->>S: Initial resources
            S->>S: Check room area / capacity and active Coaches
            S->>DB: Lock room / Coaches, read sport and facility limits
            DB-->>S: Sport compatibility and limits
            alt initial resource, sport or limit invalid
                S->>DB: Roll back transaction
                S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
            else initial resources valid
                S->>DB: Create provisional class, sport link, requirement snapshot and Coach assignments
                DB-->>S: Class
                S->>B: createScheduleBatchInTx(tx, classId, roomId, schedules)
                activate B
                B->>B: Validate 1 to 500 future non-overlapping slots
                B->>DB: Lock assignment / resources, read room capability, Coach scope / expertise / leave
                DB-->>B: Resource context
                B->>B: validateResources and require exactly one class sport
                B->>DB: Read global room / class / Coach overlaps and applicable terms
                DB-->>B: Existing schedules and covering terms
                B->>B: Lock terms, assertCanScheduleInTerm and reject conflicts
                alt schedule validation fails
                    B-->>S: AppError before session insertion
                    S->>DB: Roll back provisional class and assignments
                    S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
                else every schedule valid
                    B->>DB: classSchedule.createMany(status SCHEDULED)
                    DB-->>B: Insert count
                    B-->>S: schedulesCreated
                    S->>DB: Commit class, assignments and all sessions
                    S-->>C: Class, sport and schedulesCreated
                end
                deactivate B
            end
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: sendCreated or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 201 created plan or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show created count or failure, refresh successful planner data
%% NESTING_EXCEPTION: request, sport-mode, initial-resource and schedule guards require four frames.
%% Guard groups short-circuit, errors skip later work. DB insertion failure aborts transaction, never confirms success.
%% UI currently omits termId, server auto-selects covering non-CLOSED facility or global terms.
%% ADMIN / RECEPTIONIST fail authorizeExact(MANAGER). Manager cannot create a new global sport here.
